#. Key:	BuildMode.Straight
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.Straight"
msgid "Straight"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.Default
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.Default"
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.Default.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.Default.Desc"
msgid "Quadratic Bezier curve: the end heads along the line from the start, the mouse wheel turns it."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.Zoop
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.Zoop"
msgid "Zoop"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.Zoop.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.Zoop.Desc"
msgid "Straight on out of the start, keeping its direction and slope: level from a foundation edge or a free start, the road's own slope from a road end. Move the aim along the road to set the length; it stops on the longest road allowed."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.Smooth
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.Smooth"
msgid "Smooth quadratic Bezier"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.Smooth.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.Smooth.Desc"
msgid "Quadratic Bezier curve (like the default mode), and the height eases in and out, matching the slope of the roads it connects. Up to 45 degrees."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.CutFences
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.CutFences"
msgid "Cut also fences"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.CutFences.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.CutFences.Desc"
msgid "Also cuts this road's fences at the same place: road fences standing on it and fence walls on its edges (stacked walls too). Other roads and their fences are left alone. Train tracks and vehicle paths on the road are always cut."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.RoadMode
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.RoadMode"
msgid "Road Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	BuildMode.RoadMode.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,BuildMode.RoadMode.Desc"
msgid "Builds this blueprint's road along a road you draw (start, end, curves, like the road tool), with the blueprint's fences, fence walls and walking paths beside it all the way."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_1x.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_1x.Name"
msgid "Road (1 wide)"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_1x.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_1x.Desc"
msgid "A road one foundation wide, with asphalt on top and concrete sides. Click the start, click the end: it curves like a vehicle path, snaps to road ends and foundation edges, and the mouse wheel turns it. Hold the snap key and aim at a built road (or an intersection curb) to build a road right beside it, edge to edge and flush, in one click. Press Alt to turn the road limits off or on (off: up to 1 km long, any turn or slope, the build gun reaches 1 km; remembered). Lines are set in the customizer (Road Lines). Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_2x.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_2x.Name"
msgid "Road (2 wide)"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_2x.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_2x.Desc"
msgid "A road two foundations wide, with asphalt on top and concrete sides. Click the start, click the end: it curves like a vehicle path, snaps to road ends and foundation edges, and the mouse wheel turns it. Hold the snap key and aim at a built road (or an intersection curb) to build a road right beside it, edge to edge and flush, in one click. Press Alt to turn the road limits off or on (off: up to 1 km long, any turn or slope, the build gun reaches 1 km; remembered). Lines are set in the customizer (Road Lines). Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_3x.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_3x.Name"
msgid "Road (3 wide)"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_3x.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_3x.Desc"
msgid "A road three foundations wide, with asphalt on top and concrete sides. Click the start, click the end: it curves like a vehicle path, snaps to road ends and foundation edges, and the mouse wheel turns it. Hold the snap key and aim at a built road (or an intersection curb) to build a road right beside it, edge to edge and flush, in one click. Press Alt to turn the road limits off or on (off: up to 1 km long, any turn or slope, the build gun reaches 1 km; remembered). Lines are set in the customizer (Road Lines). Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_4x.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_4x.Name"
msgid "Road (4 wide)"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Road_4x.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Road_4x.Desc"
msgid "A road four foundations wide, with asphalt on top and concrete sides. Click the start, click the end: it curves like a vehicle path, snaps to road ends and foundation edges, and the mouse wheel turns it. Hold the snap key and aim at a built road (or an intersection curb) to build a road right beside it, edge to edge and flush, in one click. Press Alt to turn the road limits off or on (off: up to 1 km long, any turn or slope, the build gun reaches 1 km; remembered). Lines are set in the customizer (Road Lines). Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadCut.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadCut.Name"
msgid "Cut Road"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadCut.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadCut.Desc"
msgid "Aim at a road: the orange outline shows where it is cut. Click to split it there into two roads that keep its curve, lines and paint; train tracks and vehicle paths on it are cut too. Build mode \"Cut also fences\" also cuts the road's own fences at the same place (white outlines). Free."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadSplit.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadSplit.Name"
msgid "Split Road"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadSplit.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadSplit.Desc"
msgid "Aim across a road 2 or more wide: the cyan line shows where it is split lengthwise, in steps of 8 m. Click to replace it with two roads side by side that keep its curve, lines and paint (a 2 wide road becomes two 1 wide roads, a 4 wide one for example 1 + 3). Free."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadJoin.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadJoin.Name"
msgid "Join Road"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadJoin.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadJoin.Desc"
msgid "The opposite of Cut Road. Aim near where two roads meet end to end: the green outline shows the joined road; click to replace the two with one road along both, with the aimed road's lanes, material and paint. They must be the same width, continue smoothly into each other and follow the one curve a single road would have (two pieces of a cut road always do; a straight piece and a curved one cannot be joined), and the joined road must not be too long. Markings, paths, tracks and fences stay where they are. Free."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadMerge.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadMerge.Name"
msgid "Merge Road"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadMerge.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadMerge.Desc"
msgid "The opposite of Split Road. Click a road to pick it (white outline), then click the road right beside it: edge to edge, at the same height, starting and ending together. The green outline shows the merged road; click to replace the two with one road of their combined width (at most 4 wide), with the first road's lanes, material and paint (side lines on if either had them). Markings, paths, tracks and fences stay where they are. Click the picked road again to drop it. Free."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadAdjust.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadAdjust.Name"
msgid "Adjust Curvature"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadAdjust.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadAdjust.Desc"
msgid "Orange circles mark the road ends near you. Click one to grab that end (and the end of the road joined to it, when two roads meet end to end), then move it like a road end: the mouse wheel turns it, the snap key snaps it to a free road end, hold H to nudge it. The roads follow as holograms; click again to replace them with the new curves, keeping their other ends, lines and paint. Ends joined to an intersection stay. Free."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceCut.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceCut.Name"
msgid "Cut Fence"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceCut.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceCut.Desc"
msgid "Aim at a road fence or fence wall: the orange outline shows where it is cut. Click to split it there into two that keep its course, side, material and paint. Hold the snap key near a road end (for example where the road was cut) to snap the cut in line with it. Nothing else is cut. Free."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceJoin.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceJoin.Name"
msgid "Join Fence"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceJoin.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceJoin.Desc"
msgid "The opposite of Cut Fence. Aim near where two road fences or fence walls meet end to end: the green outline shows the joined fence; click to replace the two with one fence along both, with the aimed fence's side, material and paint. They must be the same kind (and look), have the road on the same side, continue smoothly into each other and follow the one curve a single fence would have (two pieces of a cut fence always do; a straight piece and a curved one cannot be joined). Any length up to 1 km. Free."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_GuardRail.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_GuardRail.Name"
msgid "Guard Rail"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_GuardRail.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_GuardRail.Desc"
msgid "Metal guard rail. Aim at a road to follow its edge. Hold the snap key and aim at another road fence to replace it. Cost is per 4 m."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_Jersey.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_Jersey.Name"
msgid "Cement Blocks"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_Jersey.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_Jersey.Desc"
msgid "Concrete road barrier. Aim at a road to follow its edge. Hold the snap key and aim at another road fence to replace it. Cost is per 4 m."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_Grid.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_Grid.Name"
msgid "Metal Grid Fence"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_Grid.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_Grid.Desc"
msgid "Metal grid fence. Aim at a road to follow its edge. Hold the snap key and aim at another road fence to replace it. Cost is per 4 m."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_GridTall.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_GridTall.Name"
msgid "Steel Mesh Fence Wall"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	Fence_GridTall.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,Fence_GridTall.Desc"
msgid "4 m steel frame with a diamond wire mesh. Aim at a road to follow its edge (centred on the edge), or at an intersection to follow its curb; aim at the upper or lower half of a fence wall to stack another above or below it, or hold the snap key to replace it. Cost is per 4 m."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Concrete.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Concrete.Name"
msgid "Concrete Fence Wall"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Concrete.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Concrete.Desc"
msgid "4 m concrete wall, 0.5 m thick. Aim at a road to follow its edge (centred on the edge), or at an intersection to follow its curb; aim at the upper or lower half of a fence wall to stack another above or below it. Can be painted. Cost is per 4 m."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Ficsit.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Ficsit.Name"
msgid "FICSIT Fence Wall"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Ficsit.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Ficsit.Desc"
msgid "4 m FICSIT wall, 0.5 m thick. Aim at a road to follow its edge (centred on the edge), or at an intersection to follow its curb; aim at the upper or lower half of a fence wall to stack another above or below it. Can be painted; the customizer's Material tab switches between concrete, FICSIT and steel. Cost is per 4 m."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Sign.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Sign.Name"
msgid "Sign Wall"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Sign.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Sign.Desc"
msgid "4 m wall, 0.5 m thick, that shows a sign design along its whole road side, repeated every 8 m (the design of an 8 x 4 m billboard). Press E on it to edit the design with the game's sign editor. Aim at a road to follow its edge, or at an intersection to follow its curb; scroll with the snap key held to turn it round; aim at the upper or lower half of a fence wall to stack another above or below it. Ends and top in matte metal, circuit grooves on the back. Cost is per 8 m, like a Small Billboard."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Steel.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Steel.Name"
msgid "Steel Fence Wall"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	FenceWall_Steel.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,FenceWall_Steel.Desc"
msgid "4 m steel wall, 0.5 m thick. Aim at a road to follow its edge (centred on the edge), or at an intersection to follow its curb; aim at the upper or lower half of a fence wall to stack another above or below it. Can be painted; the customizer's Material tab switches between concrete, FICSIT and steel. Cost is per 4 m."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	SignGantry.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,SignGantry.Name"
msgid "Sign Gantry"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	SignGantry.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,SignGantry.Desc"
msgid "Two steel columns on the fence lines of a road and a beam across it, at least 8 m above the road. Aim at a road and click to put it across, then the mouse sets the height of the beam (every 2 m) and a second click builds it. Aim a sign at the beam or a column to put it flat on that face, every 2 m (scroll turns it 45 degrees). Cost is per 8 m of steel."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	LaneArrow.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,LaneArrow.Name"
msgid "Lane Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	LaneArrow.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,LaneArrow.Desc"
msgid "Paints an arrow on a lane of a road. Aim at a road: it snaps to the middle of the lane you aim at and points the way you are looking along the road. The mouse wheel picks the arrow (straight, left, right, straight or left, straight or right, left or right). It takes the colour of the road's lane lines (the cyberpunk road's glow too); repaint it with the paint gun, or change its look in the customizer's Material tab. Dismantle it on its own or with the road. Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	LaneNumber.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,LaneNumber.Name"
msgid "Lane Number"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	LaneNumber.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,LaneNumber.Desc"
msgid "Paints a single digit (0 to 9) on a lane of a road, for speed limits and lane numbers. Aim at a road: it snaps to the middle of the lane you aim at and reads upright for traffic driving the way you are looking along the road. The mouse wheel picks the digit. It takes the colour of the road's lane lines (the cyberpunk road's glow too); repaint it with the paint gun, or change its look in the customizer's Material tab. Dismantle it on its own or with the road. Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	LaneVehicle.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,LaneVehicle.Name"
msgid "Lane Vehicle"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	LaneVehicle.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,LaneVehicle.Desc"
msgid "Paints a vehicle's map icon (Tractor, Truck, Explorer, Factory Cart or Cyberwagon) on a lane of a road, to mark lanes for one kind of vehicle. Aim at a road: it snaps to the middle of the lane you aim at and points the way you are looking along the road. The mouse wheel picks the vehicle. It takes the colour of the road's lane lines (the cyberpunk road's glow too); repaint it with the paint gun, or change its look in the customizer's Material tab. Dismantle it on its own or with the road. Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	WalkingPath_2m.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,WalkingPath_2m.Name"
msgid "Walking Path (2 m)"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	WalkingPath_2m.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,WalkingPath_2m.Desc"
msgid "A walking path two metres wide: concrete blocks on top, concrete sides, one dashed middle line. Hold the snap key and aim at a road (or an intersection curb) to build it right beside the road, edge to edge and flush, along its whole length: with one on each side, a 1-wide road becomes 1.5 foundations wide, and fences snap to the path's outer edge. Click the start, click the end to build one on its own; it snaps to walking path ends. No vehicle paths, tracks or lane markings on it. Nudge it up for a raised sidewalk. The look (Concrete Blocks, Asphalt, Cyberpunk) is set in the customizer's Material tab, the middle line in Road Lines. Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	WalkingPath_4m.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,WalkingPath_4m.Name"
msgid "Walking Path (4 m)"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	WalkingPath_4m.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,WalkingPath_4m.Desc"
msgid "A walking path four metres wide: concrete blocks on top, concrete sides. Hold the snap key and aim at a road (or an intersection curb) to build it right beside the road, edge to edge and flush, along its whole length: one on a side of a 1-wide road makes it 1.5 foundations wide, and fences snap to the path's outer edge. Or click the start, click the end: it snaps to 4 m walking path ends and to road ends every 2 m across. No vehicle paths, tracks or lane markings on it. Nudge it up for a raised sidewalk. Split Road makes two 2 m paths of it. The look (Concrete Blocks, Asphalt, Cyberpunk) is set in the customizer's Material tab; Road Lines adds a middle line and side lines. Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadIntersection.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadIntersection.Name"
msgid "Road Intersection"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadIntersection.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadIntersection.Desc"
msgid "Click free road ends (or free intersection ends) to pick them, up to 6, then click away from them to build: they are joined with curved curbs. Click a picked end again to drop it. Side lines are set in the customizer (Road Lines > Sidelines). Free to build."
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadFill.Name
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadFill.Name"
msgid "Gap Fill"
msgstr ""

#. Key:	RoadFill.Desc
#: Content/Text/ST_RoadMaker.uasset
msgctxt "RoadMakerAssets,RoadFill.Desc"
msgid "Fills the gap between roads with road surface, at their height. Click road, walking path and intersection edges around the area, in any order: they are cut where they cross, or joined by straight lines, and a yellow line closes the shape where the edges do not meet. Click inside the shape to build it. Click a picked edge again to drop it. It takes the look of the first edge's road; the customizer's Material tab and paint change it. Free to build."
msgstr ""

